{"title":"Satellite&#8217;s Ring of Fire Solar Eclipse Photo Taken From Orbit","link":"https://kottke.org/26/02/satellites-ring-of-fire-solar-eclipse-photo-taken-from-orbit","date":1772143137000,"content":"\n         \t<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/img-48450-01.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none//images/posts/01/img-48450-01.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/img-48450-01.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1500\" height=\"1500\" /></p>\n\t<p>During the recent annular solar eclipse on February 17, the ESA’s PROBA-2 satellite captured <a href=\"https://www.esa.int/ESA_Multimedia/Images/2026/02/Annular_solar_eclipse_seen_from_space\">this great shot</a> of the Moon passing in front of the Sun. Cue up the Johnny Cash.\n</p>\n \n\n        \n         <p><strong>Tags:</strong> <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/astronomy\">astronomy</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/Moon\">Moon</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/photography\">photography</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/science\">science</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/Sun\">Sun</a></p>\n        \n    ","author":"Jason Kottke","siteTitle":"Kottke","siteHash":"89a883271b4598f9b33ebe87be70d38557bcd266e68aee521a8f93622e0ab723","entryHash":"c2e7c8fe7123f7c0089091562ea935a42c0df3d3eba6b1710a860ed2f3dd77bb","category":"Sites"}